# This directory is the `python/` root of the aws-xray-sdk Lambda layer asset.
#
# It is committed empty (this .keep) on purpose: `SudokuStack` references
# `build/xray-layer` as a `lambda_.Code.from_asset(...)` layer, and `cdk synth`
# (and the offline template-assertion suite) stages this local directory at
# synth time. That staging only needs the directory to EXIST — it does not need
# the third-party wheels present — so keeping this placeholder lets the offline
# suite synthesize with no network and no `pip install`.
#
# The actual dependencies (aws-xray-sdk + wrapt) are installed here by
# `just build-layer` (which `just deploy` runs first). That step needs PyPI and
# is therefore a deploy-time concern, never part of the offline `just test`.
#
# The installed wheels themselves are git-ignored (see .gitignore `build/` plus
# the `build/xray-layer/python/*` re-ignore); only this .keep is tracked, so the
# asset path always resolves. `just build-layer` clears the installed packages
# but preserves this file.
